WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.110
Different TV producers and filmmakers have
offered up their own takes on the spooky family

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:09.680
created by cartoonist Charles Addams - and
some have worked a lot better than others.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.019
Here, then, is every major Addams Family movie
and TV series iteration, ranked in order from

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.080
worst to best.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:23.120
The 2019 animated The Addams Family is everything
no Addams Family project has ever been: loud,

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.460
fast, bright, and moralizing.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.680
This movie feels less like an expansion of
the Addams universe and more like a lesser

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:35.140
Tim Burton animated project, or a knockoff
of Adam Sandler's Hotel Transylvania movies.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:40.399
The characters are given an unnecessary and
clunky origin story: After an angry mob breaks

00:00:40.399 --> 00:00:44.520
up the wedding of Gomez and Morticia because
they're too weird, the loving couple runs

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.699
away to New Jersey, with Thing in tow.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:51.179
They take up residence in an abandoned asylum,
where they recruit mental patient Lurch to

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:51.960
be their butler.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:56.429
Flash forward into the future, and the Addams
have lived in sad isolation for more than

00:00:56.429 --> 00:00:57.000
a decade.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:01.260
There's also an awkward plot about a reality
TV host wanting to get rid of this family

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:05.400
that isn't bothering anybody and how Wednesday
befriends that host's tween daughter.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.660
And, of course, there's a lesson about how
it's a good thing to be yourself.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:14.760
The New Addams Family inadvertently gives
away its premise in its title: It's the same

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:18.120
old Addams Family as the 1960s sitcom, it's
just... new.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.440
It plays like a less-than-great eerie remake
of its predecessor, with many of the actors

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:26.450
not so much interpreting their characters,
but imitating their counterparts from the

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:27.620
'60s series.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.420
"Gomez, Mrs. Bell from the PTA just called
me."

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.060
"I hate obscene phone calls."

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:37.630
At least they had the good sense to bring
in original Gomez John Astin as occasional

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:42.290
character Grandpapa Addams, but his presence
just reminded viewers of the greatness that

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:43.180
once was.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:47.160
The only true innovation of The New Addams
Family is that it seemed to take a cue from

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:51.680
the early '90s Addams Family movies and gave
much more screen time to Wednesday and Pugsley.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:58.540
This early '90s animated cash-in on the popular
live-action movies aired on ABC Saturday mornings,

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:00.760
so it's obviously geared toward children.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:05.300
But the people who made it focused so hard
on having it be squeaky clean that they lost

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.200
the spirit of what makes the Addams Family
special.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:13.340
"Those screams were half-hearted, and I didn't
hear his usual joyous cackle."

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:18.380
Sure, the Addamses live in a creepy, shadowy
mansion, and yes, Wednesday and Uncle Fester

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:22.510
like to blow stuff up whenever they get the
chance, but the show leans too heavily on

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:26.580
the family's interactions with the outside
world and its suffocating normalcy.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:32.020
At least The Addams Family: The Animated Series
restores and updates the 1960s sitcom version's

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:36.670
iconic, snap-happy theme song and draws inspiration
from the rich, busy look of the 1991 Addams

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:38.280
Family film.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:43.860
This first animated take on The Addams Family
combines the charmingly grotesque look of

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:48.959
Charles Addams' creations with the voices
and vaudevillian interplay of '60s TV Gomez

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:54.080
and Morticia, all mixed in with the trappings
and clichés of '70s Saturday morning cartoons.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:59.220
That is to say, the animation is cheap and
stilted, there are wacky animal sidekicks,

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.900
and every joke is met with a braying laugh
track.

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:07.000
"That's odd.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:10.040
I never realized this was a music cue."

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:14.920
This Addams Family feels an awful lot like
Scooby-Doo, Where Are You?-— they even crossed

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:18.920
over at one point - only it embraces the spooky
instead of unmasking it.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:24.120
Like the Mysteries, Inc. gang, this version
of the Addams Family also drives around endlessly,

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:28.290
not in a van but a "Creepy Camper," which
looks like they miniaturized their mansion

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:29.700
and put it on top of a hearse.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:34.959
They cause a stir in a new location in every
episode, and, true to Addams Family spirit,

00:03:34.959 --> 00:03:39.069
they're oblivious to how the way they do things
is not the way the rest of the world does

00:03:39.069 --> 00:03:39.560
things.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:45.840
When Raul Julia, the actor who played Gomez
Addams in the hit '90s films, passed away,

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:49.460
the chance for a successful Addams Family
trilogy seemed to be lost.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:54.319
What fans eventually got was Addams Family
Reunion, a franchise reboot in the form of

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:55.620
a direct-to-video movie.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:04:00.180
It doesn't stand up to the other films in
its decidedly B-level production values.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:04.930
The plot is a little weak too, involving the
Addamses attending the incorrect family reunion

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:08.660
by mistake and getting mixed up in a guy's
killing-for-inheritance scheme.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:13.120
While it lacks a lot of the dark comedy and
joyful playfulness of the two Addams Family

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:17.320
movies that preceded it, it's agreeable and
family-friendly, and the filmmakers wisely

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:22.190
cast the great Tim Curry in the role of Gomez,
while Daryl Hannah turns in a serviceable

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:22.940
Morticia.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:29.000
There were a lot of weird sitcoms in the '60s,
and many of them were built around fish-out-of-water

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:29.720
scenarios.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:34.140
The Addams Family took a different approach:
let the water come to the fish.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:39.300
The Addams lived in a gigantic 19th century
mansion full of sentient plants, suits of

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:43.730
armor, a lion, and more, enjoying each other's
company and occasionally dealing with the

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:48.200
stuffy local conservative figures who populated
the generic town outside its doors.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:53.380
They also casually tossed off references to
death, darkness, and the macabre, which certainly

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:55.320
wasn't happening on Gilligan's Island.

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:58.560
"This is going to be the greatest train wreck
in railroad history.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:01.100
I'm going to switch them onto the same track."

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:06.150
Morticia knits or paints while Gomez fences,
checks his stocks, and deals mildly in the

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:10.120
dark arts, which occurs between the couple's
ferocious displays of affection.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:14.639
If Charles Addams' original creations were
meant to be a thorough contrast to the strictures

00:05:14.639 --> 00:05:17.510
of modern life, the TV series helped get the
point across.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:23.490
When the Addams Family made the leap to the
big screen in 1991, all the Addams' quirks

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:27.160
and the franchise's tropes were amped up without
taking it too far.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:32.289
Morticia is more elegant and enigmatic than
ever, Gomez is bursting with a zest for life

00:05:32.289 --> 00:05:33.240
- and death.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:38.040
Uncle Fester is downright frightening, and
Wednesday is just casually, unflinchingly

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:39.800
interested in torture and mayhem.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:47.280
[Electric chair sounds]

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:53.390
These characters are allowed to finally embrace
the behaviors and activities only hinted at

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:57.560
in other Addams Family media, while the film's
big budget affords a realistically rendered

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:01.979
Thing, which expressively darts around the
Addams' gloriously well-appointed but decaying

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:02.480
mansion.

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:07.140
Moreover, the prevailing message of Addams
Family shows of the past is more clearly conveyed

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:10.820
in both The Addams Family and 1993's Addams
Family Values.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:13.220
The people in this family aren't the creeps.

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:19.380
It's the modern world, with its forced cheerfulness
and scams with a smile, that's truly villainous.

